From c89075c80601943f5cb2a159585870970294bade Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 12:52:25 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Execution settings: --execution cpu|gpu|mixed and the
 location of each phase

A single choice places the computations, declared by
declareDefaultOptions and read by initialize:

- `--execution cpu` (`-x`): no device, all the computations on the host;
- `--execution gpu`: device `gpu` of MFEM (CUDA or HIP, as MFEM is built),
  all the computations on the GPU;
- `--execution mixed`: device `gpu` of MFEM, each phase placed on the CPU
  or on the GPU (GPU by default) by `--finite-elements` (`-fe`),
  `--behaviours` (`-bh`), `--linear-solver-device` (`-lsd`) and
  `--post-processings` (`-ppd`), refused in the other modes.

The settings (`getExecutionSettings`) give the default values of the
parameters choosing the computations (BehaviourIntegration, the
computations of the gradients, of the inner forces and of the tangent
operator, the computation of the post-processings), below the parameters
and the environment variables; the device of MFEM (`--device` refused if it
contradicts the mode); the memory of hypre (on the host when the linear
solvers are on the CPU, `--hypre-on-host` refused if it contradicts it).
The behaviour libraries (behaviour integrators and point wise models) and
the linear solvers and preconditioners are checked against them: a library
or a solver computing elsewhere is refused, with the options accepting it.
The solvers of MFEM compute where the device of MFEM computes, the solvers
of hypre where its memory is. Without `--execution`, nothing changes.

ExecutionSettingsTest: the settings read, the device and the memory of
hypre, a uniaxial tension of a cube computed with the default parameters
in the cpu and gpu modes and in the 16 combinations of the mixed mode
(stress known, finite elements, behaviours and post-processings computed
where placed, observed by the counters of the computations by kernels and
by the location of the integration), refusal of the libraries and of the
solvers computing elsewhere, and of the contradictory options (8 cases).
Mutations of the default values, of the checks and of the memory of hypre
are detected. CPU suite 195/195.
