+.. _mfem_mgis_batch_computations_execution:
+
+Execution settings
+------------------
+
+The option :code:`--execution` (or :code:`-x`), declared by
+:code:`mfem_mgis::declareDefaultOptions` and read by
+:code:`mfem_mgis::initialize`, places all the computations with a single
+choice:
+
+- :code:`cpu`: no device, all the computations on the host;
+- :code:`gpu`: device :code:`gpu` of :code:`MFEM` (:code:`CUDA` or
+  :code:`HIP`, as :code:`MFEM` is built), all the computations on the GPU;
+- :code:`mixed`: device :code:`gpu` of :code:`MFEM`, each phase being
+  placed on the CPU or on the GPU (:code:`gpu` by default) by
+  :code:`--finite-elements` (:code:`-fe`: gradients, inner forces, tangent
+  operator), :code:`--behaviours` (:code:`-bh`: integration of the
+  behaviours), :code:`--linear-solver-device` (:code:`-lsd`: linear
+  solvers and memory of hypre) and :code:`--post-processings`
+  (:code:`-ppd`). These options are refused in the other modes.
+
+All the combinations of the mixed mode are supported. The settings give:
+
+- the default values of the parameters choosing the computations:
+  :code:`BehaviourIntegration` is :code:`Batch` if the finite elements or
+  the behaviours are on the GPU; :code:`GradientsComputation`,
+  :code:`InnerForcesComputation` and :code:`TangentOperatorComputation` are
+  :code:`Kernels` if the finite elements are on the GPU; the
+  post-processings are computed by kernels if they are on the GPU. A
+  parameter given to a problem, or an environment variable giving its
+  default value, takes precedence;
+- the device of :code:`MFEM`: :code:`--device` may still give a
+  configuration of the device (for instance :code:`ceed-cuda`), refused if
+  it contradicts the mode (a GPU with :code:`cpu`, no GPU with
+  :code:`gpu` or :code:`mixed`);
+- the memory of hypre: on the host if the linear solvers are on the CPU
+  (as :code:`--hypre-on-host`, which can't contradict the settings).
+
+The behaviour libraries and the linear solvers are checked against the
+settings, since they decide where they compute:
+
+- a behaviour placed on the GPU requires a library generated by the
+  :code:`generic-parallel` interface of :code:`MFront` with a GPU backend,
+  a behaviour placed on the CPU a library computing on the host;
+- the direct solvers :code:`MUMPSSolver` and :code:`UMFPackSolver` compute
+  on the CPU, :code:`AmgX`, :code:`AmgXPCG` and :code:`CuDSSSolver` on the
+  GPU, the solvers of hypre where its memory is, and the solvers and
+  smoothers of :code:`MFEM` where the device of :code:`MFEM` computes (on
+  the GPU in the :code:`gpu` and :code:`mixed` modes).
+
+A library or a solver computing elsewhere than the settings place it is
+refused, with a message giving the options which would accept it. Without
+:code:`--execution`, nothing changes: the computations are placed by the
+other options, the parameters and the environment variables. The settings
+are returned by :code:`mfem_mgis::getExecutionSettings`.
+
 Selection of the device
 -----------------------
 
